# Target C-II — simple-wall support-six `H5` exclusion by projection potentials

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** proved candidate awaiting independent audit; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** the ten noncollapsed simple-wall support-six reciprocal `H5` sign/order orbits  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_support6_h5_wall_projection_potential_2026_09_18.py`

This note eliminates the ten simple ground-collinearity-wall cases left after
the exact support-six `H5` reduction. Together with the uniform exclusion note,
it closes the entire uniform and simple-wall noncollapsed `H5` metric branch.
It does not address the collapsed support-six branch. Higher-codimension walls
are covered only to the extent of the separate promoted double-wall exclusion.

The dependency chain is

```text
simple-wall H5 finite reduction + double-wall exclusion
  -> ten exact zero-aware chirotope/sign representatives
  -> all weak rank-3 extensions at a generic projection infinity
  -> no acyclic signed projection constraint graph
  -> contradiction with full signed unit-force equilibrium
  -> simple-wall H5 eliminated.
```

## Zero-aware projection-potential lemma

The summed equilibrium identity is the same as in the uniform case. For any
scalar potential `a` and generic projection vector `u`,

\[
 0=\sum_i a_i\,u\!\cdot F_i
  =\sum_{ij\in E}s_{ij}(a_i-a_j)
    \frac{u\!\cdot(y_i-y_j)}{|y_i-y_j|}.
\tag{1}
\]

If the signed constraint graph defined by the projection order and the edge
signs is acyclic, a strict topological potential makes every summand positive.
Therefore every generic projection order of a metric equilibrium must contain a
directed cycle.

The wall has one reciprocal collinearity, so its ordinary point chirotope has a
zero triple. This does not invalidate the argument: a generic `u` still gives a
strict total order of all seven reciprocal points. Adjoining the formal point
`U` at infinity gives a rank-three chirotope extension with no new zero triple
involving `U`. The correct weak Grassmann--Plücker condition is that the three
products either vanish identically or contain both signs. The certificate uses
this zero-aware condition, not the strict uniform test.

## Exact finite result

The existing wall verifier supplies ten canonical representatives, all with a
simple wall of type `036` after the allowed symmetries. For each representative,
the certificate enumerates all `7!` possible generic projection orders, assigns
the signs of the point-at-infinity triples, and checks every eight-element
rank-three weak chirotope axiom. Thus every realizable metric projection is in
the tested overapproximation.

The numbers of weak rank-three infinity extensions are

\[
\boxed{138,128,124,136,136,132,134,120,120,120},
\]

and the number of acyclic signed projection graphs is zero in every case.
Consequently no simple-wall representative can satisfy the full signed
unit-force equilibrium.

This is an exact finite sign certificate: no coordinates, floating-point
thresholds, or numerical nonlinear solver are used.

## Consequence and remaining obstruction

Within the current noncollapsed support-six reduction, the six uniform and ten
simple-wall `H5` branches are now excluded. The remaining support-six endpoint
is the collapsed branch

\[
 y_1=\cdots=y_6\ne0,
\]

whose local two-dimensional closure family has already been certified. That
local family cannot be excluded by repeating the six local pentagon, turn-gap,
parallel-anchor, or no-extra-contact tests. A global stopped-train,
source-embedding, source-separation, diameter-bar/KKT, or source-preserving
finite-motion argument is still required.

**Disposition:** proved candidate awaiting independent audit; all ten simple-wall
metric cases closed within the stated full-equilibrium hypotheses; C-II remains
open because the collapsed branch remains live.
